assertion  XSH.iswxdigit.001
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswxdigit() returns non-zero for each character
           of the class xdigit as the locale definition lists it: the ten
           digits, A to F and a to f.
test       t/001-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswxdigit.002
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale iswxdigit() returns 0 for each of these
           characters, which the locale definition does not place in the
           class: the letters G to Z and g to z, the punctuation, the
           white-space characters and the controls.
test       t/002-non-members.c

assertion  XSH.iswxdigit.003
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       iswxdigit(WEOF) is within the domain and returns 0, since WEOF is
           not a character of the class.
test       t/003-weof.c

assertion  XSH.iswxdigit.004
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       Each of the 22 hexadecimal digit characters is also an alnum
           character; the ten decimal digits are digit characters and the
           twelve letters are alpha characters.
test       t/004-xdigit-relations.c

assertion  XSH.iswxdigit.005
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iswxdigit.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1
class      required
says       In a UTF-8 locale iswxdigit() is non-zero for the 22 hexadecimal
           digit characters and 0 for every other ASCII-range character
           (xdigit has only those members in every locale).
note       Needs an installed multibyte UTF-8 locale (NOTINUSE otherwise);
           only ASCII-range characters are examined.
test       t/005-utf8-portable.c
